OL,3,GCentral, Tayside & Fife
OL,4,
OL,5,CToday:FA cloudy morning with some
OL,6,Fshowers, but these slowly dying out.
OL,7,FDry in the afternoon with bright or
OL,8,Fsunny spells developing. Feeling
OL,9,Frather cool for August.
OL,10,
OL,11,CTonight:FIt will be a dry evening with
OL,12,Fsunny spells. Skies becoming mostly
OL,13,Fclear overnight and turning chilly,
OL,14,Fespecially in the glens.
OL,15,
OL,16,CSaturday:FA chilly start then a dry
OL,17,Fand bright day. The best of the sunny
OL,18,Fspells in the east.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
